From: hashtagbasit
Subject: drm/panel: il97680a: start the Retroid Pocket Nova panel dark

The init sequence set the panel to its maximum brightness (0x0d75) before
any frame was sent, so the Nova flashed white or grey on every mode set
(boot, power off, switching between Game and Desktop Mode) until
drm_panel_enable() put the user's brightness back. Start at 0; the
backlight comes up to the user's level once video flows. Found by
lavachemist (PB OS).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-il97680a.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-il97680a.c
@@ -110,8 +110,13 @@
 
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, MIPI_DCS_WRITE_CONTROL_DISPLAY,
 				     0x20);
+	/*
+	 * Start dark: this runs before any frame is sent, so a lit panel
+	 * shows white until then. drm_panel_enable() turns the backlight up
+	 * to the user's level once video flows.
+	 */
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, MIPI_DCS_SET_DISPLAY_BRIGHTNESS,
-				     0x0d, 0x75, 0x00, 0x00);
+				     0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00);
 
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_exit_sleep_mode_multi(&dsi_ctx);
 
